      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellery%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town takes its name from William Ellery, a signer of the Declaration of Independence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellery%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "European settlers first arrived around 1806, long before the town’s official establishment.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellery%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ellery’s east shore of Chautauqua Lake was developed early as a tourist and recreational spot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellery%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Southern Tier Expressway, carrying I‑86 and NY‑17, crosses Chautauqua Lake at Bemus Point within Ellery.",
